const body = `<h1>4.6a — Dungeon Loop: Combat While Loop</h1>

<p>
    <strong>Type:</strong> RPG Integration. You've studied while loops, for loops,
    nested loops, and loop analysis. Now you put all four concepts into one system:
    a dungeon crawler where combat uses while loops and room exploration uses
    for loops. This is a 3-day assignment.
</p>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity rpg">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">RPG Build</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~25 min</span>
    </div>

    <h3>The Goal</h3>

    <p>Create a <code>DungeonLoop.java</code> class. Today you build the combat
    engine — a while-loop that keeps two combatants fighting until one falls.
    You already wrote combat logic in Unit 3's Combat.java. Now you wrap it in a
    loop that runs an unknown number of rounds.</p>

    <p>Open the <a href="../docs/unit-04/dungeon-system.html">Dungeon Loop System
    (Student RPG Guide)</a>. Follow the specification for Part 1: runCombat().</p>

    <h3>Part 1: runCombat() — The While Loop</h3>

    <p>Create <code>DungeonLoop.java</code>. Add this method:</p>
    <pre><code>public static boolean runCombat(String playerName, int playerHP, int playerAC,
                                int playerAttackBonus, String monsterName,
                                int monsterHP, int monsterAC,
                                int monsterAttackBonus, int monsterDamageDie)</code></pre>

    <p><strong>Requirements:</strong></p>
    <ul>
        <li>Print a combat header: <code>"=== COMBAT: [player] vs [monster] ==="</code></li>
        <li>Use a <code>while</code> loop. Condition: <code>playerHP > 0 && monsterHP > 0</code></li>
        <li>Each iteration: print current HP, player attacks, monster counterattacks
            (only if still alive)</li>
        <li>Attack pattern: roll d20, add bonus. Natural 20 = critical (d8 × 2).
            Total ≥ AC = hit (d8). Otherwise miss.</li>
        <li>After loop: return <code>true</code> if player won, <code>false</code> otherwise</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="socratic">
        <h3>Socratic Checkpoint</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>You don't know how many rounds this fight will last. Why is this
                a while loop and not a for loop? What's the rule for choosing?</li>
            <li>Why does the monster only counterattack when <code>monsterHP > 0</code>?
                What would happen if you removed that check?</li>
            <li>Trace through one round: player attacks, damage is subtracted, then
                monster attacks. Does the order matter? What if the monster went first?</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="tinker">
        <h3>Tinker: Variable Damage</h3>
        <p>
            Right now both sides roll d8 for damage. Make the player's damage die
            a parameter too. Then make the monster's critical hit do double damage
            (dmgDie × 2 on a natural 20). Does the fight feel more dangerous?
        </p>
    </div>

    <p><strong>Acceptance Test:</strong></p>
    <pre><code>boolean result = DungeonLoop.runCombat("Hero", 20, 14, 3, "Goblin", 10, 12, 2, 6);
System.out.println("Result: " + (result ? "Won" : "Lost"));
// Run 5 times. Verify combat ends when one side hits 0 HP.
// Verify the boolean matches the winner.</code></pre>
</div>

